WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720 line:88%
Deaf community life continued after graduation.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.780 line:88%
Living near a deaf school, attending churches, joining Deaf

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.120 line:88%
clubs and associations, and gathering at conventions or sports

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.020 line:88%
events helped people remain connected.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.660 line:88%
A school can begin a network of relationships.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.620 line:88%
Community institutions help those relationships continue across time and

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.320 line:88%
distance.

00:00:18.908 --> 00:00:22.668 line:88%
Cochlear implants brought another debate about access and identity.

00:00:23.268 --> 00:00:27.308 line:88%
The medical perspective emphasizes access to hearing and spoken

00:00:27.308 --> 00:00:28.008 line:88%
communication.

00:00:28.608 --> 00:00:31.908 line:88%
The cultural concern emphasizes the possible loss of signed

00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:34.828 line:88%
language and community when hearing and speech become the

00:00:34.828 --> 00:00:35.648 line:88%
central goals.

00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:39.208 line:88%
These are different ways of evaluating the consequences of

00:00:39.208 --> 00:00:39.908 line:88%
intervention.

00:00:40.477 --> 00:00:43.337 line:88%
In the early nineteen nineties, many Deaf opponents of

00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:46.017 line:88%
implantation feared the loss of their language and culture.

00:00:46.237 --> 00:00:49.017 line:88%
They saw Deaf life as fulfilling, rather than a

00:00:49.017 --> 00:00:50.177 line:88%
defect needing treatment.

00:00:50.777 --> 00:00:53.557 line:88%
Most deaf children are born to hearing parents, so

00:00:53.557 --> 00:00:56.697 line:88%
choices about language and intervention often involve parents who

00:00:56.697 --> 00:00:58.317 line:88%
did not grow up in Deaf culture.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.610 line:88%
The lecture’s closing account describes a less intense negative

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.930 line:88%
reaction than in the early nineteen nineties, while retaining

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:08.190 line:88%
debate about implantation in young children.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.250 line:88%
This is a historical account in the twenty twenty-three

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:11.710 line:88%
deck.

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:15.530 line:88%
To understand the disagreement, keep auditory access and cultural

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:16.990 line:88%
continuity visible together.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:21.230 line:88%
A device decision also raises questions about language, relationships,

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.110 line:88%
and belonging.
